# Every path operator with 0 to 40 operands, the counts the format allows
# and those it does not. Glyph 1 + 2 * (41 * OP + N) runs OP with N operands
# after a moveto to (100, 100); the glyph after it then draws lines of
# 3000 right and 3000 down, so its box shows the current point the
# operator leaves. Operators, in order: rlineto, hlineto, vlineto, rrcurveto, hhcurveto, hvcurveto, vhcurveto, vvcurveto, rcurveline, rlinecurve, flex, hflex, hflex1, flex1, rmoveto, hmoveto, vmoveto.
glyph
  endchar
end
glyph # rlineto 0
  100 100 rmoveto  rlineto endchar
end
glyph # rlineto 0, then the current point
  100 100 rmoveto  rlineto 3000 0 rlineto 0 -3000 rlineto endchar
end
